    "title": "Museum of Transportation hosts event with 'Top Gun: Maverick' advisor - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Ledford ,\n45 minutes ago\nKIRKWOOD, Mo. – It was a full agenda Wednesday night at the National Museum of Transportation as their guest of honor’s top-flight resume includes being an advisor to one of Hollywood’s biggest block busters.\nRetired U.S. Navy Captain Kevin McLaughlin shared his stories of aviation. The veteran of 33-years is a former Commander of TOPGUN, the U.S. Navy fighter weapons school.\nHe also served as an advisor to the box-office smash “Top Gun: Maverick,” which grossed close to $1.5 billion worldwide.\n“You know, we’re always trying to recruit the next generation of naval aviators,” McLaughlin said. “And I know we have some young, hopeful naval aviators in the crowd.”\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nDaily News Kirkwood resident Cate Ward brought her 10-year-old son, Cal, with her.\n“Cal’s always been really interested in fighter jets and vehicles and military vehicles, all of those things,” Ward said. “So we knew when he was really little with all the Legos and stuff that this was going to be an interest for him.”\n“I think it’s just really cool because I like seeing them fly by and how loud they are,” Cal added.\nMcLaughlin, who lived in the area for three years during the early 2020s, still has fond memories of the film.\n“Especially I’ll sit on an airplane, somebody’s watching it and I’ll kind of kind of chuckle at a certain scene or a certain plot plotline and think back to how that was developed and what my role was at the time,” he said.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
